1
00:01:38,359 --> 00:01:39,480
Taipei pays handsomely.

2
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,760
Either US dollars or small gold Buddhas.

3
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,920
Quite lavish.

4
00:01:43,359 --> 00:01:44,319
Even I was tempted.

5
00:01:45,079 --> 00:01:47,640
Boss Zhu said he was being crude,

6
00:01:48,159 --> 00:01:49,239
just worried he fell short on courtesy.

7
00:01:50,239 --> 00:01:51,760
Still, he's admired you from afar for so long,

8
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:52,760
and really just wants to meet you.

9
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:55,120
We'll meet when the time is right.

10
00:01:55,879 --> 00:01:56,799
Leave it to fate.

11
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,760
Taking the bait without biting the hook.

12
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,159
This sea fishing...

13
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:10,199
is all about patience.

14
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,199
You have to stay focused.

15
00:02:14,919 --> 00:02:16,240
Better drink some of this,

16
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:21,719
so you stay sharp enough to watch the float.

17
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:23,280
And don't go cursing.

18
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,759
It isn't easy for the fish, either.

19
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,000
Risking its life to take the bait.

20
00:02:27,719 --> 00:02:28,520
A little mutual understanding, right?

21
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,560
The intel on Institute 761—

22
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,639
I don't care how you get it,

23
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:33,080
but it must pass through my hands.

24
00:02:33,719 --> 00:02:35,159
You have your mission, and I have mine.

25
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,599
Let's share it for a win-win.

26
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,280
What an enormous appetite.

27
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,439
Come on, just bite the hook already.

28
00:04:11,879 --> 00:04:14,080
Something you risked everything to get

29
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:15,199
should fetch a high price.

30
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,600
One copy isn't enough.

31
00:04:17,439 --> 00:04:19,439
If I were you, I'd sell two.

32
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,040
Don't ask questions you shouldn't.

33
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,079
Keep making the money you're making.

34
00:04:25,199 --> 00:04:26,319
Deliver to whoever you're supposed to.

35
00:04:27,279 --> 00:04:29,439
Give an extra copy to me, and that's extra cash.

36
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,800
You studied math.

37
00:04:31,079 --> 00:04:32,160
Double the income.

38
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,839
You can do the math, right?

39
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:35,839
Make money or go to prison.

40
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,120
Make your choice.

41
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:43,040
One more thing.

42
00:04:43,319 --> 00:04:44,879
Don't go to the Pacific anymore.

43
00:04:44,879 --> 00:04:45,680
It's not safe.

44
00:04:46,439 --> 00:04:47,439
Tell them to change the venue.

45
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:49,160
If you get any more good stuff,

46
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:50,720
remember to call this number.

47
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,000
I'll head out first.

48
00:04:52,399 --> 00:04:53,480
Leave five minutes after me.

49
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,519
You're back.

50
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:48,959
What are you doing?

51
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,360
What time did you get back today?

52
00:05:52,639 --> 00:05:53,759
Going out again tonight?

53
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:58,639
By the way,

54
00:05:58,839 --> 00:06:00,959
I took that bottle of liquor yesterday.

55
00:06:00,959 --> 00:06:01,879
Remind me later

56
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:02,639
to buy another one.

57
00:06:02,639 --> 00:06:04,240
I won't be drinking at night anymore.

58
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:07,439
Also, either aim better,

59
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,759
or wipe the toilet seat when you're done.

60
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,879
I don't have time to clean it.

61
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,000
You didn't cook tonight?

62
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:21,399
Have you eaten?

63
00:06:21,879 --> 00:06:22,920
How have things been lately?

64
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,040
Does she still trust you?

65
00:06:25,879 --> 00:06:27,360
Do we have any paste at home?

66
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,160
Help me look for some.

67
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:29,639
I have to put these up tomorrow.

68
00:06:32,519 --> 00:06:33,879
Qiutian lost her cat.

69
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,560
During my business trip,

70
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,680
I saw many numbers she often uses.

71
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:41,600
I tried them all on Lin Kanshan's email,

72
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:43,160
but none of them worked.

73
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:56,000
Got a minute? Let's talk.

74
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,000
Go ahead.

75
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,720
I have three minutes left.

76
00:07:00,879 --> 00:07:02,720
Lin Kanshan is almost done with his instant noodles.

77
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,480
I just feel like...

78
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,040
...a dual-police family is pretty interesting.

79
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,439
As husband and wife,

80
00:07:07,439 --> 00:07:09,160
we only know each other's one phone number.

81
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:12,199
To be honest,

82
00:07:12,879 --> 00:07:14,319
do you have other numbers,

83
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:15,319
other jobs,

84
00:07:15,319 --> 00:07:16,360
other identities,

85
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,399
or even other names?

86
00:07:17,399 --> 00:07:18,319
I don't know any of it.

87
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,560
If you left in anger one day,

88
00:07:20,639 --> 00:07:22,279
I wouldn't know if you left for work

89
00:07:22,519 --> 00:07:23,680
or because we had a fight.

90
00:07:27,279 --> 00:07:28,680
All I can do is wait around like a fool.

91
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,360
I know.

92
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,160
It's not like I'm new to the job either.

93
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,240
I should understand.

94
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,720
But don't you think...

95
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:42,959
...maybe between the two of us, we should...

96
00:07:47,319 --> 00:07:48,279
Should what?

97
00:07:50,519 --> 00:07:51,160
Never mind.

98
00:07:54,959 --> 00:07:56,319
If you want to say something, make it quick.

99
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,439
I have one minute left.

100
00:07:57,959 --> 00:07:59,639
Lin Kanshan is almost done with his instant noodles.

101
00:08:00,959 --> 00:08:02,319
Forget it. We'll talk later.

102
00:08:07,959 --> 00:08:08,839
Are you hungry?

103
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,800
Want me to make some noodles?

104
00:08:13,319 --> 00:08:15,319
I'll go. You take over monitoring for me.

105
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,079
Getting close to her,

106
00:08:31,079 --> 00:08:33,440
isn't it also for intelligence on Lin Kanshan?

107
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:35,039
Is all this trouble really necessary?

108
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,840
I know investigation work is exhausting,

109
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,799
tough, and far from easy.

110
00:08:48,399 --> 00:08:50,039
But Comrade He Chunxiao,

111
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:52,080
our work is also very hard

112
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,240
and very challenging.

113
00:08:54,879 --> 00:08:56,360
As a colleague,

114
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,440
please respect my work and my profession.

115
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,159
Thank you.

116
00:09:00,279 --> 00:09:01,360
That's not what I meant.

117
00:09:15,639 --> 00:09:16,360
On the morning of the third,

118
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,360
I'm meeting the secretary of Gulou District Hospital.

119
00:09:18,919 --> 00:09:20,399
We're still divided on what we discussed last time.

120
00:09:21,039 --> 00:09:21,639
It can't be delayed any longer.

121
00:10:11,279 --> 00:10:12,320
The first rule of tailing...

122
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,840
...is never treat your target like a fool.

123
00:10:13,879 --> 00:10:15,000
A vantage point you think is good,

124
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:15,919
he'll think so too.

125
00:10:15,919 --> 00:10:17,600
A spot you pick, anyone else would pick it too.

126
00:10:18,679 --> 00:10:19,240
So keep adapting.

127
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,559
Catch him off guard.

128
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,200
Forget what the books say.

129
00:10:23,399 --> 00:10:24,639
The simplest way

130
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:26,360
is to never let him spot you.

131
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,519
Memorize the terrain.

132
00:10:30,679 --> 00:10:32,039
Stay out of his line of sight.

133
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:32,759
Take shortcuts,

134
00:10:32,879 --> 00:10:34,320
and wait for him ahead on the other side.

135
00:10:46,519 --> 00:10:47,120
Sometimes,

136
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:49,200
someone will walk into a dead end and wait.

137
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,679
If you foolishly follow them in

138
00:10:50,679 --> 00:10:51,559
and lock eyes,

139
00:10:51,759 --> 00:10:52,960
you've basically blown your cover.

140
00:10:53,279 --> 00:10:55,279
Just like in chess or cards, you lose.

141
00:11:25,919 --> 00:11:26,960
Hats can be changed back and forth.

142
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:27,960
Clothes can also be changed back and forth.

143
00:11:28,039 --> 00:11:29,639
Only shoes can never be changed back and forth.

144
00:12:12,879 --> 00:12:13,360
Hey, man.

145
00:12:13,759 --> 00:12:14,519
Where are you headed?

146
00:12:14,879 --> 00:12:15,759
I'm going to Xiaguan.

147
00:12:15,759 --> 00:12:17,159
Great! I urgently need to send something over.

148
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:19,000
It's Chinese medicine. A friend needs it urgently.

149
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:20,279
I can't get away right now.

150
00:12:20,279 --> 00:12:21,159
I'll give you ten yuan.

151
00:12:21,159 --> 00:12:21,919
Could you do me a favor?

152
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:23,559
Sure.

153
00:12:23,679 --> 00:12:24,360
This rain...

154
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,399
It's going to pour even harder soon.

155
00:12:25,559 --> 00:12:26,240
Put this on.

156
00:12:26,399 --> 00:12:27,080
Give me that umbrella.

157
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:27,840
The umbrella's too small.

158
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:28,639
Here, take it.

159
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:33,559
Let me tell you the address.

160
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,759
Right at the first T-junction in Xiaguan,

161
00:12:35,759 --> 00:12:36,519
there's a temple.

162
00:12:36,559 --> 00:12:37,600
Someone will be waiting there.

163
00:12:37,799 --> 00:12:38,799
Just hand the medicine over to him.

164
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:40,120
Leave it to me.

165
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:40,679
Great, great.

166
00:12:40,679 --> 00:12:41,799
Thank you. Thanks a lot.

167
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:46,600
Is this your medicine?

168
00:13:33,360 --> 00:13:34,480
Looking for me?

169
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:36,639
And you?

170
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,720
Were you waiting for me?

171
00:13:40,559 --> 00:13:41,679
What's the matter?

172
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,240
You came to meet someone,

173
00:13:43,639 --> 00:13:45,480
so of course I should wait on you.

174
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:48,080
You have a good memory.

175
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,320
Just an offhand remark of mine,

176
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,600
and you remember it so clearly.

177
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,279
Good company rubs off.

178
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,759
If I didn't improve around you, Brother Qi,

179
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,879
how could I live up to your trust?

180
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:00,679
Things I can remember,

181
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,159
others can remember too.

182
00:14:02,759 --> 00:14:04,879
If you don't bring that kid into business,

183
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,559
won't he just tag along anyway?

184
00:14:09,399 --> 00:14:10,200
No rush.

185
00:14:10,879 --> 00:14:12,360
Unless his wings have grown and he can fly.

186
00:14:13,039 --> 00:14:14,919
Better safe than sorry.

187
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,320
If he moves faster than before

188
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:20,120
and we don't even know it, that's trouble.

189
00:14:23,559 --> 00:14:25,360
Boss Ding took over that land of yours;

190
00:14:25,679 --> 00:14:27,320
he'll hand over both the staff and the plant.

191
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:28,639
You two can negotiate the exact price.

192
00:14:29,039 --> 00:14:29,919
Business is business.

193
00:14:30,039 --> 00:14:30,960
Don't take advantage of him, either.

194
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:32,440
As long as everyone is happy.

195
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,240
He's as sly as a fox.

196
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:37,720
Would he even be willing to talk?

197
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:40,960
Regarding Xiao Lu's case,

198
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:42,519
I've basically found out everything.

199
00:14:42,679 --> 00:14:43,759
Burglary,

200
00:14:43,759 --> 00:14:44,840
involving a massive sum,

201
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:45,759
trafficking in intelligence,

202
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:46,919
endangering national security.

203
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:48,480
Combining the two charges,

204
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,960
he won't get out within ten years.

205
00:14:53,159 --> 00:14:54,519
Brother Qi, you've helped me so much.

206
00:14:55,039 --> 00:14:57,559
How could I ever repay all these gifts?

207
00:14:58,840 --> 00:14:59,600
We're partners.

208
00:15:00,039 --> 00:15:01,480
That's how business works.

209
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,159
You help me, and I help you.

210
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,919
Under reform and opening up, we make money together.

211
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:07,120
When you opened, I came empty-handed.

212
00:15:07,559 --> 00:15:09,240
Today I'm making up for all the gifts.

213
00:15:09,879 --> 00:15:11,639
If you really feel bad about it,

214
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,919
then just buy me a roast chicken.

215
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:34,320
A gentleman in Taipei received a letter.

216
00:15:35,039 --> 00:15:36,960
He knows who lives at that address.

217
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:40,519
I heard Taiwan, China once offered ten million NT dollars

218
00:15:40,519 --> 00:15:41,639
to buy this address,

219
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,000
as well as his photo.

220
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,240
So that means

221
00:15:45,799 --> 00:15:47,879
you've successfully spent that money.

222
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,080
If you have time,

223
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,720
he'd like to meet with you.

224
00:15:52,759 --> 00:15:55,360
The mainland, Hong Kong, China, Macau, China, Japan...

225
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,399
Anywhere works.

226
00:15:57,559 --> 00:15:58,879
You decide the time and place.

227
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:02,000
Tell him to wait a bit longer.

228
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:05,000
We're all in business.

229
00:16:05,159 --> 00:16:05,759
Just like when we sell

230
00:16:05,759 --> 00:16:06,240
CT scanners

231
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,000
or MRI machines,

232
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,879
things only last when they develop naturally.

233
00:16:09,559 --> 00:16:10,360
Don't be in such a rush.

234
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:15,320
Meeting each other...

235
00:16:15,759 --> 00:16:17,279
there has to be a good pretext.

236
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:19,600
We have plenty of time.

237
00:16:20,399 --> 00:16:21,600
Today we're getting reacquainted

238
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,600
and deepening our ties.

239
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,600
We can take our time and treat each other like brothers.

240
00:16:26,919 --> 00:16:28,519
As for Wen Zongshu's containers,

241
00:16:29,039 --> 00:16:31,360
let them keep smuggling what needs to be smuggled.

242
00:16:31,639 --> 00:16:32,879
Don't go there again for now.

243
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,360
Don't shut down the channel either.

244
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:35,720
Otherwise, someone will get suspicious.

245
00:16:37,759 --> 00:16:39,159
Before I return to Taiwan, China,

246
00:16:40,559 --> 00:16:42,679
that piece of yarn on the mailbox by the door...

247
00:16:43,399 --> 00:16:44,480
was that yours?

248
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,120
I just like making friends.

249
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,279
Having someone owe you a favor

250
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:53,440
is far better than making an enemy.

251
00:17:01,159 --> 00:17:05,039
Then who are Chunxiao and Jinlan?

252
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:07,920
Chunxiao is my cousin,

253
00:17:08,079 --> 00:17:09,000
and Jinlan is his wife.

254
00:17:09,519 --> 00:17:10,359
Whoever you say they are,

255
00:17:10,359 --> 00:17:11,160
that's who they are.

256
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:13,559
If you say they aren't, they aren't.

257
00:17:19,559 --> 00:17:20,319
I'm off.

258
00:18:01,759 --> 00:18:02,400
Brother Shan.

259
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:03,920
Are you at the bureau?

260
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:05,279
Did Ma Qi just get back?

261
00:18:06,119 --> 00:18:06,839
Yeah.

262
00:18:06,839 --> 00:18:08,160
He's getting ready to interrogate A-Cai.

263
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,000
Why are you so late?

264
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:11,039
You didn't even ask for leave.

265
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,319
When are you getting here?

266
00:18:12,319 --> 00:18:13,200
I'm heading back right now.

267
00:18:29,079 --> 00:18:29,920
Xiao Lin.

268
00:18:31,319 --> 00:18:32,200
Xiao Lin.

269
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:40,240
Xiao Lin.

270
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:43,240
Xiao Lin!

271
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:53,279
Where have you been?

272
00:18:53,279 --> 00:18:54,319
Look at the state you're in.

273
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,119
I was tailing someone.

274
00:18:58,240 --> 00:18:59,160
Did it have to be today?

275
00:19:00,319 --> 00:19:02,519
No choice. He picked today.

276
00:19:03,039 --> 00:19:05,279
Meeting in the rain leaves no trace.

277
00:19:10,599 --> 00:19:12,079
I thought you overslept,

278
00:19:12,079 --> 00:19:13,359
and was wondering whether to wait.

279
00:19:14,039 --> 00:19:15,759
Not bad. I'm not late.

280
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,359
Sleepless nights are the norm,

281
00:19:17,359 --> 00:19:18,480
but I always get up,

282
00:19:18,839 --> 00:19:20,519
especially when there's work to do.

283
00:19:21,839 --> 00:19:23,119
You don't look well.

284
00:19:23,359 --> 00:19:24,640
Take some Chinese medicine when you can.

285
00:19:24,799 --> 00:19:25,680
Clear the heat and dryness,

286
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:26,519
calm your nerves, dispel the dampness.

287
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:28,960
Sure. Unless the herbs aren't dry

288
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:29,960
and only make the dampness worse.

289
00:19:36,319 --> 00:19:37,599
You have three minutes to change.

290
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,039
I'll wait for you at the residential surveillance site.

291
00:19:53,319 --> 00:19:54,359
Xiao Lin

292
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:55,839
Mimi

293
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,079
Xiao Lin

294
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:01,119
Mimi

295
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:06,359
Xiao Lin

296
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,160
Xiao Lin

297
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:10,680
Mimi

298
00:20:14,839 --> 00:20:15,400
Xiao Lin

299
00:20:18,039 --> 00:20:18,839
Xiao Lin

300
00:20:47,759 --> 00:20:49,039
Cats are just like people.

301
00:20:50,799 --> 00:20:52,240
It's all about fate.

302
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,559
If we could find it, we'd have found it by now.

303
00:20:57,039 --> 00:20:57,799
Forget it.

304
00:20:58,960 --> 00:20:59,960
Let's stop looking.

305
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:18,359
Put simply,

306
00:21:18,599 --> 00:21:20,119
you're definitely not getting out anytime soon.

307
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:21,839
Staying silent won't do you any good.

308
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,839
Better to lay everything out on the table,

309
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:24,920
and see whether you stay detained here with me

310
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,119
or get transferred to Public Security.

311
00:21:26,839 --> 00:21:28,160
I can't offer you comfort,

312
00:21:28,359 --> 00:21:29,559
but I can save you some suffering.

313
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:36,480
You're a smart man.

314
00:21:36,839 --> 00:21:37,960
You know how to work the angles.

315
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,759
You know that by regulation,

316
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:40,880
a single interrogation session

317
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:42,400
can't exceed six to eight hours.

318
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,359
If I really wanted to play hardball,

319
00:21:44,519 --> 00:21:45,960
I could bend the rules, too.

320
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,200
Give you a thirty-second break,

321
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,319
then dive right back into questioning.

322
00:21:50,039 --> 00:21:50,759
Of course,

323
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,559
I could just grind it out with you,

324
00:21:53,079 --> 00:21:54,599
but I've got a lot on my plate lately.

325
00:21:54,599 --> 00:21:56,200
I have to stay bedside at the hospital,

326
00:21:56,319 --> 00:21:58,200
so my patience is running a bit thin.

327
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:00,880
We all know your track record.

328
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:04,000
You're quite somebody around Minzhong.

329
00:22:04,240 --> 00:22:06,200
Someone chopped your hand off in your youth,

330
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,039
and you still never backed down.

331
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:09,079
So let's lay our cards on the table.

332
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:10,240
I'll give you two options.

333
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:11,440
Option one: come clean,

334
00:22:11,759 --> 00:22:12,880
and spare us both the grief.

335
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:14,599
Option two: I go all the way

336
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,440
and wear you down to the bitter end.

337
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:17,319
Choose.

338
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:18,599
Which path?

339
00:22:22,599 --> 00:22:23,559
No strength.

340
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,160
Can't walk.

341
00:22:30,559 --> 00:22:31,680
Out of strength? Then eat.

342
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:32,920
Consider this a friendly gesture.

343
00:22:33,279 --> 00:22:34,960
I packed this meal myself.

344
00:22:35,079 --> 00:22:36,039
Guaranteed strictly vegetarian.

345
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,440
It's still hot. Eat up.

346
00:22:56,559 --> 00:22:57,359
Go ahead and eat.

347
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:07,519
I'm being completely sincere.

348
00:23:07,799 --> 00:23:08,960
Why put yourself through this?

349
00:23:10,519 --> 00:23:11,680
If I were willing to talk,

350
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:13,920
I wouldn't have to eat bugs.

351
00:23:14,960 --> 00:23:16,279
To tell you the truth,

352
00:23:17,119 --> 00:23:18,559
this has nothing to do with you.

353
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:21,160
The things I've been doing out there...

354
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:22,519
if I were to talk,

355
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:23,880
a lot of people would go down.

356
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:25,839
Me going inside and suffering alone

357
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:28,079
is better than so many people suffering.

358
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:29,759
You know what I mean?

359
00:23:33,759 --> 00:23:34,640
But that business with the police...

360
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,799
...really is tough to handle.

361
00:23:38,839 --> 00:23:40,000
Go get Lao Wei over here.

362
00:23:42,359 --> 00:23:43,200
Hurry up!

363
00:23:43,559 --> 00:23:44,359
The boss isn't here.

364
00:23:44,359 --> 00:23:45,720
Can the two of us really make this call?

365
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,480
Everything I've said

366
00:24:17,359 --> 00:24:18,240
is completely sincere.

367
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:21,000
You said someone would suffer if you talked.

368
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:23,599
You tore down a 91-year-old widow's home,

369
00:24:23,599 --> 00:24:24,680
where she lived her whole life,

370
00:24:24,680 --> 00:24:26,079
and cheated her out of her life savings.

371
00:24:26,720 --> 00:24:27,799
Did she not suffer?

372
00:24:30,799 --> 00:24:33,000
Did you know the old lady jumped to her death yesterday?

373
00:24:41,079 --> 00:24:42,240
I'm asking you one last time:

374
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:43,599
are you going to talk or not?

375
00:24:53,720 --> 00:24:54,519
This way, this way.

376
00:24:56,079 --> 00:24:57,079
Chief Wei, this way.

377
00:24:57,319 --> 00:24:57,880
Wu Jiali.

378
00:24:58,640 --> 00:24:59,240
Chief Wei.

379
00:24:59,799 --> 00:25:01,200
The suspect's chin is injured.

380
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,400
His mouth was also cut by a spoon.

381
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:03,000
It's quite a mess.

382
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:04,079
Where's Ma Qi?

383
00:25:04,279 --> 00:25:05,240
Has he lost his mind?

384
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,680
He's in the interrogation room.

385
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:45,519
As required,

386
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,839
I will read out

387
00:25:48,480 --> 00:25:49,519
the disciplinary decision.

388
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:51,519
Go ahead.

389
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:52,759
Comrade Ma Qi:

390
00:25:52,920 --> 00:25:54,079
In accordance with relevant regulations

391
00:25:54,359 --> 00:25:56,680
and deliberation by the Bureau Party Committee,

392
00:25:57,119 --> 00:25:59,039
it is hereby decided to suspend you

393
00:25:59,039 --> 00:26:01,079
from duty pending investigation.

394
00:26:01,240 --> 00:26:02,079
During the suspension,

395
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:03,839
you must immediately cease

396
00:26:03,839 --> 00:26:06,119
performing your current duties

397
00:26:06,119 --> 00:26:07,920
and cooperate with the investigation as required.

398
00:26:08,119 --> 00:26:10,759
If you contest this suspension decision,

399
00:26:10,759 --> 00:26:13,480
you may, within 30 days of receiving this notice,

400
00:26:13,640 --> 00:26:15,799
submit to the Bureau's Discipline Inspection Commission

401
00:26:15,920 --> 00:26:17,480
or a higher competent authority

402
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:18,799
a formal written appeal.

403
00:26:19,039 --> 00:26:20,400
During the appeal period,

404
00:26:20,559 --> 00:26:22,440
this decision shall remain in effect.

405
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:24,359
Upon conclusion of the investigation,

406
00:26:24,359 --> 00:26:26,000
based on the findings,

407
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,279
a final decision will be issued separately.

408
00:26:29,319 --> 00:26:31,160
Please accept the organization's decision properly

409
00:26:31,559 --> 00:26:32,960
and actively cooperate with the investigation.

410
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:35,119
Minzhong State Security Bureau.

411
00:26:40,039 --> 00:26:41,359
Do you have anything to say?

412
00:26:42,359 --> 00:26:43,559
I wish to tender my resignation.

413
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,279
I ask for the organization's approval.

414
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:53,759
No one is perfect.

415
00:27:54,279 --> 00:27:56,200
Even legends have weaknesses.

416
00:27:56,799 --> 00:27:57,559
They lie, too.

417
00:27:58,279 --> 00:27:59,200
And they can fall under suspicion.

418
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:02,759
Go on.

419
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:04,880
Ma Qi told me

420
00:28:05,559 --> 00:28:06,799
he was terrified the mole

421
00:28:06,799 --> 00:28:07,799
was Li Fengge.

422
00:28:08,599 --> 00:28:10,200
I'm also terrified he's compromised.

423
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:13,359
The more I think about it, the harder it is to shake.

424
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:14,759
Just like right now.

425
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:17,079
What if extracting that confession was intentional?

426
00:28:17,160 --> 00:28:18,400
Losing control of his emotions on purpose?

427
00:28:18,519 --> 00:28:20,519
Deliberately breaking discipline with severe consequences?

428
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:21,960
What if he got suspended on purpose?

429
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:23,160
What's the goal?

430
00:28:25,839 --> 00:28:26,880
And what's the motive?

431
00:28:27,599 --> 00:28:29,240
He sensed some kind of danger.

432
00:28:36,799 --> 00:28:39,599
Something seemed off during his last psych test.

433
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:42,039
The only thing I didn't expect

434
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:44,039
was that he'd be spooked so quickly.

435
00:28:44,839 --> 00:28:46,279
You only tailed him once,

436
00:28:47,279 --> 00:28:48,119
and he was already alerted.

437
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:49,960
Answer only "yes" or "no."

438
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:50,359
Understood.

439
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,400
In the past six months,

440
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:53,799
have hostile intelligence agencies approached you?

441
00:28:53,799 --> 00:28:54,400
No.

442
00:28:54,480 --> 00:28:55,480
Are you currently in a relationship?

443
00:28:55,480 --> 00:28:55,880
No.

444
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:57,519
Have you dated or thought about dating?

445
00:28:57,519 --> 00:28:58,119
No.

446
00:28:58,119 --> 00:28:59,759
Is your relationship with your family harmonious?

447
00:28:59,759 --> 00:29:00,119
No.

448
00:29:00,279 --> 00:29:01,640
Regarding the cases you handled,

449
00:29:01,799 --> 00:29:02,559
did you have any doubts?

450
00:29:02,559 --> 00:29:04,240
No. No. No.

451
00:29:04,279 --> 00:29:05,799
No. No. No.

452
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:09,519
I was worried you wouldn't let me tail him.

453
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:12,440
If a good apple is on the tree

454
00:29:13,039 --> 00:29:14,160
and you keep trying to disinfect it,

455
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:15,039
I'll stop you.

456
00:29:15,440 --> 00:29:18,079
But if it rots and falls to the ground,

457
00:29:18,160 --> 00:29:19,200
and you don't pick it up,

458
00:29:19,799 --> 00:29:22,160
the sparrows will just eat it.

459
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,559
Even someone you're closest to,

460
00:29:25,799 --> 00:29:27,279
maybe you still don't truly know him.

461
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:28,839
With so many things,

462
00:29:28,839 --> 00:29:30,559
you don't even know why they turn out like this.

463
00:29:31,079 --> 00:29:33,119
Just like in Chiung Yao's romance novels:

464
00:29:33,920 --> 00:29:35,720
no matter how much you love someone, they still leave.

465
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:36,960
Don't they?

466
00:29:37,319 --> 00:29:38,640
What if he really is compromised?

467
00:29:42,519 --> 00:29:45,759
Whether he works for us or not,

468
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:48,519
he must never work for the enemy.

469
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:52,640
So what should we do?

470
00:29:57,359 --> 00:29:58,160
What do you think?

471
00:30:37,680 --> 00:30:38,640
Xiao Lin.

472
00:30:39,920 --> 00:30:40,880
Xiao Lin.

473
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:44,000
Xiao Lin.

474
00:30:46,960 --> 00:30:47,960
Xiao Lin.

475
00:31:40,920 --> 00:31:42,759
You're half an hour later than I expected.

476
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:44,720
Had a lot on my plate today,

477
00:31:44,920 --> 00:31:46,119
so I got off work late.

478
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,799
Ah Cai really made a mess of things,

479
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:56,119
so you guys have to clean up the mess.

480
00:31:57,599 --> 00:31:58,400
So, tell me,

481
00:31:58,400 --> 00:32:00,240
how did Old Wei badmouth me behind my back?

482
00:32:01,240 --> 00:32:02,519
They say you should bring booze to a farewell.

483
00:32:02,880 --> 00:32:04,799
What do you say? Care for a drink?

484
00:32:11,319 --> 00:32:12,480
Drink if you want.

485
00:32:12,839 --> 00:32:14,079
No need for all the formalities.

486
00:32:14,440 --> 00:32:15,720
It's not like it's a funeral.

487
00:32:17,160 --> 00:32:19,160
Maybe we'll still see plenty of each other.

488
00:32:19,480 --> 00:32:19,960
Cheers.

489
00:32:20,119 --> 00:32:21,920
Not maybe. Definitely.

490
00:32:29,880 --> 00:32:31,240
The hospital is the one place in this world

491
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:33,039
that truly puts things into perspective.

492
00:32:33,359 --> 00:32:34,359
Take a walk around, and you'll realize

493
00:32:34,559 --> 00:32:36,079
everyone is equal in the face of death.

494
00:32:36,279 --> 00:32:37,240
Even suspects like A-Cai,

495
00:32:37,240 --> 00:32:38,599
who refuse to open their mouths—

496
00:32:38,599 --> 00:32:40,359
they should all be brought here to experience life.

497
00:32:40,359 --> 00:32:41,559
Go take a look at the ICU.

498
00:32:42,119 --> 00:32:43,200
How does that saying go?

499
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:45,400
It's all just an illusion.

500
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:52,000
Humans are such strange creatures.

501
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:54,680
Sometimes, before the wound has even healed,

502
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:56,359
they've already forgotten the pain.

503
00:32:56,839 --> 00:32:58,240
Once they walk out of here,

504
00:32:58,279 --> 00:33:00,039
they go right back to fighting over everything.

505
00:33:04,039 --> 00:33:04,759
Some people say

506
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:06,799
everyone's fate is predetermined,

507
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:09,480
just like a rehearsed show.

508
00:33:09,799 --> 00:33:10,559
When to take the stage,

509
00:33:10,559 --> 00:33:11,599
where to exit,

510
00:33:11,599 --> 00:33:12,960
who trips and falls,

511
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:14,200
who steps in as an understudy,

512
00:33:14,279 --> 00:33:15,480
and who gets to play the lead.

513
00:33:15,559 --> 00:33:16,519
It's all scripted.

514
00:33:16,680 --> 00:33:17,480
It can't be changed.

515
00:33:18,359 --> 00:33:19,160
Do you believe that?

516
00:33:19,759 --> 00:33:22,440
Are you talking about patients

517
00:33:22,640 --> 00:33:23,519
or criminals?

518
00:33:23,880 --> 00:33:24,799
Think about it carefully.

519
00:33:24,799 --> 00:33:25,920
Isn't it the same for everyone?

520
00:33:27,599 --> 00:33:29,000
From the day someone is born

521
00:33:29,559 --> 00:33:32,359
to the day they enter an interrogation room or OR,

522
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:35,200
it's all shaped by countless random choices.

523
00:33:35,880 --> 00:33:36,759
Just look back on your own life.

524
00:33:37,119 --> 00:33:38,200
Growing up,

525
00:33:38,200 --> 00:33:39,599
how many things did you go through?

526
00:33:39,599 --> 00:33:40,759
How many choices did you make?

527
00:33:40,839 --> 00:33:43,000
After so many twists, you ended up at the bureau,

528
00:33:43,440 --> 00:33:46,160
sitting right here talking to me at this very moment.

529
00:33:47,119 --> 00:33:47,920
It's pure coincidence.

530
00:33:48,400 --> 00:33:49,319
It's simply incredible.

531
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:51,359
That mailman,

532
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,200
people like Lin Kanshan,

533
00:33:53,359 --> 00:33:54,160
Old Xiao,

534
00:33:54,160 --> 00:33:55,559
Xiao Wu, A-Cai,

535
00:33:55,559 --> 00:33:56,559
and Li Fengge.

536
00:33:56,839 --> 00:33:57,799
Aren't they all the same?

537
00:33:59,799 --> 00:34:00,799
Yeah.

538
00:34:01,839 --> 00:34:02,960
After all these years,

539
00:34:07,200 --> 00:34:07,920
the person I was back then

540
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,920
could never have imagined who I am today.

541
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:13,559
What about you? Did you ever imagine it?

542
00:34:14,239 --> 00:34:15,760
I never think about tomorrow.

543
00:34:15,920 --> 00:34:16,920
I only focus on the present.

544
00:34:17,079 --> 00:34:18,079
Because thinking about it is pointless.

545
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:19,800
You don't even know

546
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:20,719
what will happen ten minutes from now.

547
00:34:24,719 --> 00:34:26,039
Let me tell you a story.

548
00:34:26,519 --> 00:34:27,719
When I was little,

549
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:28,719
I was pretty wild.

550
00:34:29,639 --> 00:34:32,239
Smoking, drinking, shooting pool, watching plays.

551
00:34:32,960 --> 00:34:33,880
Running around everywhere.

552
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:35,880
And there was never enough money, of course.

553
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:37,119
My dad

554
00:34:37,519 --> 00:34:39,000
definitely wouldn't give me a single cent.

555
00:34:39,920 --> 00:34:41,199
So what do you do without money?

556
00:34:42,280 --> 00:34:43,119
You can only steal it.

557
00:34:44,960 --> 00:34:47,000
Tailing, scouting, listening in.

558
00:34:48,199 --> 00:34:49,239
Eventually, I figured out

559
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:51,800
that my mom always kept her money in the same spot.

560
00:34:53,199 --> 00:34:54,519
So I started stealing from it all the time.

561
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:55,920
At first, it was fifty cents,

562
00:34:56,239 --> 00:34:57,320
then all the way up to a yuan.

563
00:34:57,719 --> 00:35:00,199
Every time I went, there was money.

564
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:01,880
And I got away with it every single time.

565
00:35:03,880 --> 00:35:04,920
I was so naive back then.

566
00:35:05,639 --> 00:35:06,800
I thought my mom had no idea.

567
00:35:07,280 --> 00:35:08,519
I thought she'd never find out.

568
00:35:14,719 --> 00:35:16,320
It's an open secret.

569
00:35:19,840 --> 00:35:21,639
She's truly a great mother.

570
00:35:23,039 --> 00:35:23,639
By the way,

571
00:35:24,239 --> 00:35:26,239
why has she been staying in neurosurgery?

572
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:28,119
A blood clot or something?

573
00:35:29,840 --> 00:35:30,800
Clots, among other things.

574
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:33,480
Lying there like this will only cause more.

575
00:35:34,599 --> 00:35:35,400
There's also a tumor.

576
00:35:36,280 --> 00:35:37,320
First it was in her abdomen,

577
00:35:37,559 --> 00:35:38,679
and now it's spread to her head.

578
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:43,280
No matter how formidable you were when young,

579
00:35:43,960 --> 00:35:44,840
what good does it do?

580
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:47,719
When you're old, you still end up lying here,

581
00:35:47,719 --> 00:35:48,880
undergoing surgery after surgery.

582
00:35:49,079 --> 00:35:50,639
I don't believe in their fatalism.

583
00:35:50,639 --> 00:35:52,239
I believe in communist atheism.

584
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:54,119
Still, I've realized one thing:

585
00:35:55,800 --> 00:35:56,920
when you're young,

586
00:35:56,920 --> 00:35:58,960
you must do everything you want to do.

587
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:01,159
That's why I speak my mind at work

588
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,920
and never mince words.

589
00:36:03,320 --> 00:36:05,280
It's not that I deliberately argue with bosses.

590
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:06,440
From starting work to retirement,

591
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:07,519
it's just a few short decades.

592
00:36:07,639 --> 00:36:09,039
Why should I constrain myself,

593
00:36:09,519 --> 00:36:10,880
unable to even speak my mind?

594
00:36:12,719 --> 00:36:14,280
Isn't that what you were talking about?

595
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:17,239
The pinnacle of the human psyche, level five:

596
00:36:17,679 --> 00:36:18,920
self-actualization.

597
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:22,280
What fourth or fifth level nonsense?

598
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:23,079
What is this, an elevator?

599
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:30,039
You said

600
00:36:31,400 --> 00:36:33,639
spies, intelligence operatives,

601
00:36:33,719 --> 00:36:35,320
and traitors committing crimes—

602
00:36:35,519 --> 00:36:38,320
they all boil down to five motives:

603
00:36:38,719 --> 00:36:42,880
money, sex, coercion, ideology,

604
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:44,480
and self-actualization.

605
00:36:45,039 --> 00:36:47,559
If someone can't be tempted by the first four,

606
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:49,800
and happens to be driven by the fifth,

607
00:36:50,480 --> 00:36:51,519
leaving no crack to exploit,

608
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:53,320
then we're in serious trouble.

609
00:36:55,599 --> 00:36:57,159
I'm not your colleague anymore.

610
00:36:57,639 --> 00:36:59,559
Why are you making me work overtime to lecture you?

611
00:37:00,239 --> 00:37:02,840
Brother Qi, all these years...

612
00:37:03,280 --> 00:37:04,800
I really should thank you.

613
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:07,360
I was the one who least wanted you to leave.

614
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:14,679
You're not dumb at all.

615
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:16,199
You're very smart.

616
00:37:17,800 --> 00:37:19,159
You've got grit, and guts too.

617
00:37:19,480 --> 00:37:20,559
Though you aren't quick on the uptake,

618
00:37:20,840 --> 00:37:21,719
you know how to make up for it.

619
00:37:22,440 --> 00:37:23,400
And you know how to flatter,

620
00:37:24,199 --> 00:37:25,480
in that subtle, quiet way.

621
00:37:27,360 --> 00:37:28,360
So let me wish you

622
00:37:28,760 --> 00:37:30,039
a boundless future.

623
00:37:35,719 --> 00:37:36,559
Brother Qi,

624
00:37:37,360 --> 00:37:39,519
all these years, I've had a question

625
00:37:39,639 --> 00:37:40,760
I never dared to ask.

626
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:44,480
Go ahead.

627
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:47,519
If one day our own interrogate our own,

628
00:37:48,840 --> 00:37:49,599
how do you do it?

629
00:37:54,639 --> 00:37:56,239
You'd need the chance to interrogate first.

630
00:38:05,119 --> 00:38:05,920
See you around.

631
00:38:09,320 --> 00:38:11,199
If it's meant to be, we'll surely meet again.

632
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:28,639
When did you wake up?

633
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:30,360
Why didn't you wake me?

634
00:38:34,519 --> 00:38:35,239
What's wrong?

635
00:38:36,639 --> 00:38:37,400
It's nothing.

636
00:38:38,800 --> 00:38:40,000
Just had a dream.

637
00:38:41,920 --> 00:38:42,480
It scared me awake.

638
00:38:44,920 --> 00:38:46,199
Dreams are always the opposite.

639
00:38:50,360 --> 00:38:51,480
What did you dream about?

640
00:38:53,519 --> 00:38:54,320
I forgot.

641
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:56,960
Getting forgetful.

642
00:38:58,440 --> 00:38:59,679
You always remember

643
00:39:00,039 --> 00:39:01,119
every penny you spend.

644
00:39:01,400 --> 00:39:02,360
"Getting forgetful"

645
00:39:02,519 --> 00:39:04,480
just means you want to forget certain things.

646
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:06,519
Want some water?

647
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:09,599
Where's the cup?

648
00:39:12,840 --> 00:39:13,559
Aren't...

649
00:39:14,039 --> 00:39:15,039
Aren't you busy?

650
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:23,360
Isn't Zhao Yazhen hospitalized too?

651
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:25,000
She had an IV drip for two days,

652
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:26,039
so she told me to relieve her.

653
00:39:26,719 --> 00:39:28,480
Where did she put the cup?

654
00:39:30,920 --> 00:39:35,360
When Yazhen miscarried back then, you weren't there.

655
00:39:36,119 --> 00:39:39,599
When I had surgery, you weren't there either.

656
00:39:41,079 --> 00:39:42,519
The year your father died,

657
00:39:43,280 --> 00:39:44,559
you were abroad.

658
00:39:45,400 --> 00:39:49,559
We could never count on you for family matters.

659
00:39:50,760 --> 00:39:52,840
I've gotten used to it.

660
00:40:03,039 --> 00:40:05,599
You never come to see me.

661
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:10,480
You never come visit me.

662
00:40:13,360 --> 00:40:14,679
Well, aren't I here now?

663
00:40:15,360 --> 00:40:18,320
How come you had time to come today?

664
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:21,360
Is everything alright?

665
00:40:24,119 --> 00:40:25,480
You don't seem senile at all.

666
00:40:25,880 --> 00:40:27,320
You're keeping score in a little notebook.

667
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:29,239
I'm fine, don't worry.

668
00:40:30,760 --> 00:40:32,519
You're even moonlighting in business now.

669
00:40:33,440 --> 00:40:35,159
You'll be even busier doing business later.

670
00:40:43,599 --> 00:40:44,480
Want an apple?

671
00:40:46,239 --> 00:40:48,440
I can't bite into those anymore.

672
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:51,239
They have to be cut into small pieces,

673
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:54,079
so I can suck on them like hard candy.

674
00:41:04,519 --> 00:41:06,079
Do you remember when I was a kid?

675
00:41:08,039 --> 00:41:09,960
I must've been at least 11 or 12.

676
00:41:10,960 --> 00:41:12,079
I used to steal money from you.

677
00:41:13,320 --> 00:41:15,079
One yuan from the cabinet in the back room.

678
00:41:15,760 --> 00:41:17,039
I'd take some every once in a while.

679
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:18,840
Why didn't you ever say anything?

680
00:41:21,199 --> 00:41:22,440
Really?

681
00:41:26,639 --> 00:41:27,920
Such a large sum of money,

682
00:41:28,199 --> 00:41:29,199
how could you forget?

683
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:30,800
You don't remember?

684
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:58,039
The following content

685
00:41:58,039 --> 00:41:59,440
is recorded for state security officers'

686
00:41:59,440 --> 00:42:00,800
technical training.

687
00:42:01,599 --> 00:42:03,039
For internal viewing only.

688
00:42:03,320 --> 00:42:05,079
Please strictly adhere to confidentiality protocols.

689
00:42:05,239 --> 00:42:06,400
Surveillance

690
00:42:06,800 --> 00:42:08,400
includes both monitoring and wiretapping.

691
00:42:09,199 --> 00:42:10,440
For this technical trade,

692
00:42:11,159 --> 00:42:13,159
the key requirement is endurance

693
00:42:13,760 --> 00:42:14,880
and perseverance.

694
00:42:15,719 --> 00:42:17,039
Because in the long run,

695
00:42:17,599 --> 00:42:19,760
it's almost the most tedious work.

696
00:42:20,360 --> 00:42:21,199
For example,

697
00:42:21,440 --> 00:42:23,199
when monitoring a suspect over time,

698
00:42:23,199 --> 00:42:25,039
someone who speaks to him every day

699
00:42:25,039 --> 00:42:26,440
is most likely not a spy.

700
00:42:26,639 --> 00:42:29,079
Someone who speaks to him once in three years

701
00:42:29,199 --> 00:42:31,119
is the target we should be most vigilant of

702
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:32,440
and suspicious of.

703
00:42:33,119 --> 00:42:34,920
The unique nature of this work...

704
00:42:34,920 --> 00:42:36,000
Take myself, for instance.

705
00:42:37,280 --> 00:42:40,039
Before and after I started working...

706
00:42:40,039 --> 00:42:40,840
Wait a second.

707
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:43,480
Looks like there's an issue with the equipment.

708
00:42:46,559 --> 00:42:48,599
We might need to record this again.

709
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,159
From where?

710
00:42:53,039 --> 00:42:54,159
From the top.

711
00:42:55,920 --> 00:42:56,440
Where are you going?

712
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:57,960
You can't even manage basic professionalism.

713
00:42:57,960 --> 00:42:59,679
Find whoever you want to record it.

714
00:43:08,119 --> 00:43:08,880
Hello, everyone.

715
00:43:08,880 --> 00:43:10,599
I'm actress Zhou Yiran.

716
00:43:10,599 --> 00:43:12,079
Please tune in to the drama series

717
00:43:12,079 --> 00:43:12,800
"Confrontation."

718
00:43:13,039 --> 00:43:15,360
It's not about what you want me to do for you.

719
00:43:15,360 --> 00:43:17,079
It's about what I want to do for you.

720
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:20,199
I need you to go back and monitor Lin Kanshan.

721
00:43:20,199 --> 00:43:21,679
She has no idea what happened

722
00:43:21,679 --> 00:43:23,480
and agreed to this without understanding a thing.

723
00:43:23,480 --> 00:43:24,239
Do you understand what I mean?

724
00:43:24,239 --> 00:43:25,800
You always talk about putting yourself in others' shoes.

725
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:26,599
If I were her,

726
00:43:26,599 --> 00:43:27,639
why would I trust you?

727
00:43:27,639 --> 00:43:29,000
Unless you treat me sincerely

728
00:43:29,000 --> 00:43:30,440
and don't deceive or trick me.

729
00:43:30,719 --> 00:43:32,079
I'd definitely choose to believe her.

730
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:34,400
Straits International Travel Agency.

731
00:43:34,400 --> 00:43:35,280
Even "International" now.

732
00:43:35,519 --> 00:43:37,480
You're working together with Jinlan.
